1
00:00:01,458 --> 00:00:03,541
Finishing Treatment

2
00:00:04,416 --> 00:00:07,250
Once your course of radiation
treatment is done,

3
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:10,750
you will be provided with instructions
and next steps.

4
00:00:11,708 --> 00:00:16,250
If your overall oncology plan
is to continue with systemic treatment,

5
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:20,625
you will meet with your medical oncologist
to discuss next steps.

6
00:00:20,750 --> 00:00:24,291
From a radiation point of view,
your follow up care will be

7
00:00:24,291 --> 00:00:28,375
with the same radiation oncologist
who planned your radiation.

8
00:00:28,833 --> 00:00:31,833
The timeline
depends on your specific treatment,

9
00:00:31,916 --> 00:00:36,291
but generally patients see their radiation
oncologist in a return visit

10
00:00:36,458 --> 00:00:40,750
2 to 3 months after treatment,
with the option to return earlier

11
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,458
or contact the office at any time
if there are pressing concerns.

12
00:00:47,958 --> 00:00:49,541
Your doctor may order labs

13
00:00:49,541 --> 00:00:52,458
or imaging to monitor
the effects of treatment.

14
00:00:52,625 --> 00:00:56,791
Typically, imaging you had prior to radiation will be repeated.

15
00:00:57,833 --> 00:01:00,833
Other possible follow up strategies include: 

16
00:01:00,958 --> 00:01:04,666
ctDNA Testing & a symptom survey.

17
00:01:05,250 --> 00:01:09,625
ctDNA testing is blood work that looks specifically for DNA

18
00:01:09,625 --> 00:01:12,625
 from your tumor that could be detected in your blood, 

19
00:01:12,625 --> 00:01:15,625
called circulating tumor DNA or ctDNA. Your doctor will talk to you more about this.

20
00:01:18,791 --> 00:01:20,625
As mentioned previously,

21
00:01:20,625 --> 00:01:25,458
any side effects of radiation that you
experienced during the course of treatment

22
00:01:25,458 --> 00:01:28,416
should begin to subside after finishing

23
00:01:28,416 --> 00:01:31,416
with gradual improvement over time.

24
00:01:31,416 --> 00:01:35,458
If you continue to note symptoms,
please let your doctor know as

25
00:01:35,458 --> 00:01:39,541
there are medications are other therapies
that can help manage them.
